{
 "steps": [
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/expectation",
   "body": [
    {
     "id": "w2sh-sse",
     "httpRequest": {
      "path": "/w2sh/sse"
     },
     "httpSseResponse": {
      "events": [
       {
        "data": "one"
       },
       {
        "data": "two",
        "delay": {
         "timeUnit": "MILLISECONDS",
         "value": 50
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "w2sh-proxy",
     "httpRequest": {
      "path": "/w2sh/stream"
     },
     "httpOverrideForwardedRequest": {
      "requestOverride": {
       "path": "/w2sh/sse",
       "headers": {
        "Host": [
         "localhost:{{port}}"
        ]
       }
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "note": "stream-phase breakpoints of a client that is not connected",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/breakpoint/matcher",
   "body": {
    "httpRequest": {
     "path": "/w2sh/stream"
    },
    "phases": [
     "RESPONSE_STREAM"
    ],
    "clientId": "w2sh-absent-client"
   },
   "mask": [
    "\"id\" : \"[^\"]+\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/breakpoint/matcher",
   "body": {
    "httpRequest": {
     "path": "/w2sh/sse"
    },
    "phases": [
     "INBOUND_STREAM",
     "RESPONSE_STREAM"
    ],
    "clientId": "w2sh-absent-client"
   },
   "mask": [
    "\"id\" : \"[^\"]+\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "note": "SSE mocks hold nothing",
   "method": "GET",
   "path": "/w2sh/sse"
  },
  {
   "sleepMillis": 200
  },
  {
   "note": "the whole log so far: no hold line for the SSE mock in either phase",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/retrieve?type=LOGS"
  },
  {
   "note": "streaming proxy: each frame goes out unheld",
   "method": "GET",
   "path": "/w2sh/stream"
  },
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/breakpoint/matchers",
   "mask": [
    "\"id\" : \"[^\"]+\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "sleepMillis": 300
  },
  {
   "note": "the registry's missing-client line and the RESPONSE_STREAM dispatch failure for each frame, in order, then the streamed forward's completion entry (`writeStreamingForwardActionResponse`: the captured body as a string, `x-mockserver-streamed` and the chunk delays; the timing block, which leaves out the time to first byte on a pooled connection, is masked); masked before them is what the previous step compared plus the forward's matching and its drift pass",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/retrieve?type=LOGS",
   "mask": [
    "(?s)^.*?(?=[^\\n]* - client w2sh-absent-client not found)",
    "\"x-mockserver-chunk-delays-ms\" : \\[ \"[0-9,]+\" \\]",
    "\"timing\" : \\{[^}]*\\}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "note": "the missing-client and dispatch-failure lines as typed entries (WARN, with their arguments)",
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/retrieve?type=LOGS&format=LOG_ENTRIES",
   "mask": [
    {
     "regex": "(?s)^.*?(?=  \\{\\n    \"logLevel\" : \"[A-Z]+\",\\n(?:    [^\\n]*\\n)*?    \"messageFormat\" : \"client w2sh-absent-client not found)",
     "replace": "<earlier entries>"
    },
    {
     "regex": "(?s)^(.*\"messageFormat\" : \"stream frame WS dispatch failed[^\\n]*\\n(?:    [^\\n]*\\n)*?  \\}).*$",
     "replace": "${1}<later entries>"
    },
    {
     "regex": "(\"epochTime\" : )\\d+",
     "replace": "${1}0"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
